From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:40:43 +0000
Subject: Add a "Site not working?" page to page info

Page info gets a row, "Site not working?", below Permissions on http
and https pages. It opens a page with the protections that most often
stop a site from working, each with a switch for this site only:

- ad blocking
- third-party cookie blocking
- safer JavaScript (JavaScript JIT off)
- screen size protection (viewport)
- keyboard size protection
- time zone protection
- pop-up blocking

A protection is listed when it is on for this site or for all sites.
Each line says in plain words what the protection does. A switch this
page cannot change says why: ad blocking off in the ad blocking
settings or allowed there for the site or a domain it belongs to, or a
third-party cookie setting decided by a policy, an extension or an
exception in Site settings.

While all of them are on, the button "Relax protections for this site"
turns off, for this site only, ad blocking, third-party cookie
blocking, safer JavaScript and the screen size, keyboard size and time
zone protections. While any of these is off for the site, the page
says that turning them back on removes the site's own exceptions and
uses the settings for all sites, and the button "Turn protections back
on" does exactly that for all of them. Pop-up blocking keeps its own
switch. Each switch sets or removes this site's exception directly.

Page info reloads the page once when it closes after any change made
in it, including a change on its cookie page, instead of each part
reloading on its own. Its cookie row and cookie page show a change
made on the new page right away.

Only per-site settings are written: content setting exceptions for the
site and its third-party cookie exception through the cookie controls.
The ad blocker's own Allowed sites list is read, never written.
Nothing is sent anywhere. The changes are ordinary site settings of
the profile the page is open in.

